 r←GetTestServerStrip ini;text
⍝ Returns the strip that tells a test server from a production server, or '' when the INI
⍝ file does not ask for one. `HtmlHeader` puts it at the very top of every page.
⍝ The text comes from the INI entry "HTMLBACKGROUND:watermark"; on https://test.tatin.dev it
⍝ reads "Tatin Test Server" for example.
⍝ "HTMLBACKGROUND:color" is ignored: the page background is part of the design. The entry is
⍝ on the list of things to be removed (see `ToDo`).
 r←''
 :If ini.Exist'HTMLBACKGROUND:watermark'
     text←⊃ini.Get'HTMLBACKGROUND:watermark'
 :AndIf 0<≢text
     r←⊂'<div id="test-server-strip">',(EscapeSpecialChars text),'</div>'
 :EndIf
